# Fluxbridge — environment variables (all optional)
# Copy to .env or export these before launching. .env is git-ignored.

# --- Tradovate accounts ---
# There are NO Tradovate credentials here. Each account is token-only and is
# configured in the dashboard under Settings -> Token Accounts (one access token
# per account). Tokens are auto-renewed via renewaccesstoken (access -> check
# token) and persisted to data/settings.json.

# --- Data directory (persist settings/tokens across deploys) ---
# NEXUSPRED_DATA_DIR=/var/data

# --- Dashboard login: Sign in with Google (recommended) ---
# Configure in the dashboard under Settings -> Security, or via these env vars.
# When a client id + secret AND at least one allowed email are set, the dashboard
# requires Google sign-in (the password below is then ignored).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=xxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@gmail.com,teammate@gmail.com
# Public base URL (for the OAuth redirect behind a proxy, e.g. Render):
# PUBLIC_URL=https://your-app.onrender.com
# Optional: pin the session-cookie signing key (else auto-generated & stored):
# SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Dashboard password (FALLBACK only, used when Google sign-in is off) ---
# DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=

# --- Server ---
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=9000

# --- Auto-updater branch (default: main) ---
# NEXUSPRED_BRANCH=main

# --- Discord signal listener (optional module) ---
# Configured entirely in the dashboard (Discord Signals tab): the user token,
# watched channel IDs, webhook targets and the dry-run switch are stored in
# data/settings.json, not here. Requires discord.py-self (in requirements.txt).
